WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.880
<v Narrator><i>Odysseus debates whether to clasp Nausicaa's knees or speak from a distance.</i>

2
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:42.890
<v Nausicaa>Stranger, you seem neither base nor witless, and Zeus deals fortune as he wills — what he gives, a man must bear. But you have come to our land now, and you shall lack neither clothing nor anything owed a hard-tried suppliant. Stand, girls — this man is no enemy; wash him where the river gives shelter, and set food and oil beside him.
